       "text": "Branding FAQs",
       "align": "center",
       "classes": []
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "accordion",
     "items": [
      {
       "q": "What is the difference between a logo and a brand?",
       "a": "<p>A logo is a single mark. A brand is the full visual system around it: logo variations, colors, fonts and the way they appear on cards, signs, social media and packaging. The logo is the foundation, and branding makes it consistent everywhere.</p>"
      },
      {
       "q": "What does a small business branding package include?",
       "a": "<p>Typically a custom logo with variations, a color palette, font choices, business cards and social media graphics, plus a short brand guide. We tailor the package to the pieces you will actually use.</p>"
      },
      {
       "q": "How much does branding cost in Austin?",
       "a": "<p>Custom logo design at Logo Design Austin is priced from $125 to $175, with supporting materials added after the logo is approved. There is no upfront charge for logo design. The $950 Business Starter Package bundles a logo, a basic website and 150 business cards.</p>"
      },
      {
       "q": "How long does a branding project take?",
       "a": "<p>First logo concepts the same day are often possible for straightforward projects after review. Supporting pieces such as cards and social headers follow once the logo is approved, and timing depends on how many items you need.</p>"
      },
      {
       "q": "Can you rebrand an existing business?",
       "a": "<p>Yes. We can refresh or redesign an existing logo and build a consistent system around it, including cleaning up an older logo or one made with AI.</p>"
      },
      {
       "q": "Will I own my brand files?",
       "a": "<p>Yes. Once the project is complete and paid, the final logo and brand files are yours to use for your business.</p>"
      }
     ],
     "classes": []
    }
   ]
  },
